WEBVTT

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:04.580
Bismillah, alhamdulillah, salatu wassalamu ala
rasulullah. Hello calculus students, today

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:10.070
we'll be taking derivatives using our first
principles formula. Let's dive right in.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:14.620
As we all should know, this is our first
principles equation. Either way, I don't

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.300
want to bore you with all the details today. I
just want to highlight two important

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:22.420
things. The first is what is our goal, right?
You could tell me, okay, the goal is

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:27.080
super easy, Ziad. The goal is just
to plug in h with 0.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:32.800
While that's true, we want to do so in a way
so that we're not left with any

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:37.160
denominators that equal 0. Because if we are
left with a denominator that equals 0,

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.980
it's the same as dividing by 0, it's the same
as an undefined number, and that's

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:45.800
game over. So we want to do algebraic
manipulation to make sure that we're not

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:50.360
dividing by any 0s. The second thing I want to
mention is this term right here.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:53.400
Because when I was first learning calculus, and
a lot of the students that come to

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:58.820
me with questions are usually super upset and
confused with this term right here. So

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:04.060
I'm going to quickly show a very easy
way to untangle this equation

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:08.100
to make it very simple and to deal with our f
of x plus h term. Let's go to the

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:13.100
first example. Here we have f of x
equals 3x squared minus

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:18.140
5x. But before we go straight to our
equation, I want to just take our f

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:23.600
of x plus h. I want to see what that equals
first, because doing this, we can just

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:28.420
plug both of these into our equation, divide
them by h, and just have one or two

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:33.780
more steps until we get our full answer,
okay? So we do this very simply

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:38.870
by every single time we have an x-term. We're
going to take this x-term out,

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:44.280
and we're going to instead input our x plus
h. What that means is anything

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:49.040
that was applied to the x whether it's a factor
whether it's a squared whether it's

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:54.100
a negative will also be applied to our x
plus h a good way to visualize

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:58.480
this is by first writing once
again your 3x squared

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:03.590
minus 5x and then what you
can do is you can

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:08.980
erase your x's and instead put bracket x

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:12.720
plus h closed bracket in both
of those spots and

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:19.000
the reason we have our bracket is because
this would apply our factor

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.840
or our power to both of our terms. If we didn't
have a bracket, it would just be

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:26.720
applied to one of them, okay? The next step we
would do here is we would expand. So

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:30.960
here I would go 3 times x squared plus

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:36.230
2xh plus h squared minus

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.190
5x minus 5h.

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:45.620
And then we can also expand that 3 into our
bracket. So we could go 3x squared

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:50.460
plus 6xh plus 3h squared minus

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:55.730
5x minus 5h and here there are no more

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:59.710
like terms every single one of these terms is a
different combination of variables

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:04.790
so we are done with this step and we
can plug in our first

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:09.450
principles derivative formula we're going to go
f prime of x here equals the limit

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:15.060
as h approaches 0 and then we can
plug in our f of x plus

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:20.560
h just like we have it in this formula so we can
go here in our numerator 3x squared

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:25.340
plus 6xh plus 3h squared minus

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:30.360
5x minus 5h and then we can expand
this guy a little bit more

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:35.440
and then just like you have in our equation
we have a negative f of x okay

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:40.180
negative f of x just means we're gonna apply a
negative to both of these terms a

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:44.860
negative multiplied by 3x squared will
give us negative 3x squared and

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:49.840
a negative multiplied by our negative 5x will
be positive because two negatives

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:53.200
equal a positive so it'll be
plus 5x here and

00:03:55.230 --> 00:04:00.820
this is all over h okay now we have some

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.960
like terms we have our a positive 3x squared and
a negative 3x squared so those can

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:09.700
cancel out and we also have a negative 5x and a
positive 5x so those can also cancel

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:14.740
out and we're gonna simplify here remove those
crossed out terms we're gonna have

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:19.680
6xh plus 3h squared minus 5h

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.740
all over h but

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:29.240
see still we can't input h of 0 here because if
we do we're gonna be left with a

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:34.380
zero in the denominator that zero will make our
whole thing undefined but luckily we

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:39.800
have an h in every term here so we can divide by
an h in every single one of these

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:44.460
terms so we can divide by h here we can divide
one h here we can divide one h here

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:49.480
becomes from h squared to just one and we can
divide one of the h's right here this

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:54.740
will give us the limit as h
approaches zero bracket

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:59.820
6x plus 3h minus
5 close bracket

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:04.470
okay one last note before we end our

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:09.670
answer here is you guys might be asking me
okay why are there brackets well the

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:13.550
reason we had brackets here and we didn't have
any brackets up here it's because

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:17.630
since this is only one fraction it can be
regarded as one term so it looks like

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:22.430
we're applying our limit as h goes to zero to just one
term but once we have three terms

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:27.270
it looks like if we didn't have these brackets
that the limit is only being applied

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:32.510
to our first number. It's the same logic
as if, for example, we see

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:33.430
this term right here.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:40.310
If this term had instead just been negative 5x
plus h, you wouldn't think that

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.310
negative 5 is being multiplied into both them.
You just think negative 5 is being

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:48.070
multiplied into that first term. So that's why
we have those brackets. Anyways, now

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:52.830
since there are no h in the denominator, we can
send our h to 0. If we send our h to

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:57.530
0, this will becomes 3 times 0, so this will
be gone, and we'll be left with

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:02.810
6x minus 5. And that is our
answer for the first one.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:08.560
Just like our first example, I want to first
start by finding our x plus h, because

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:13.320
once we do that, we can plug both of these into
our first principles equation. So

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:18.250
just like our first example, again, we're
going to put in that 2x minus 1

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:23.630
and remove that x and instead
input our x plus h. Okay,

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:28.350
here we can expand once so we can
go to square root of

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:33.430
2x plus 2h minus 1.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:38.210
And now we have both of our terms fully expanded
and we can plug them right into our

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:43.460
first principles equation. So here we're going
to have f prime of x equals the

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:48.840
limit as h approaches 0 of
our f of x plus h,

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:53.760
which is square root of 2x
plus 2h minus 1,

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:59.340
subtracted by the square root of 2x minus
1, and this is all divided by

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:04.370
h. Okay? Here, the next logical step would
be to collect our like terms,

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:07.650
but due to the fact that our

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:13.340
quote-unquote like terms have
brackets over them,

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:18.140
we can't simplify right now
because a rule of

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:23.480
square root is that if I have the
square root of 2x plus

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:28.520
2h minus 1, This does not equal
square root of 2x

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:33.840
plus the square root of 2h minus the square
root of 1. Because these two

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:38.600
are not the same, we can't split this up and
collect our like terms. And instead, we

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:44.080
have to pull a tool from our mathematical
toolbox, okay? This tool is

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:49.160
almost always used when you're dealing with
square roots and fractions. And it's

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:54.300
called multiplying by a conjugate. A simplified
explanation just for our application

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:58.650
here a conjugate is when you
multiply by a fraction

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:03.960
and this fraction is gonna have the same
numerator and denominator so it equals

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:09.170
1 just like how we know that 4 over 4
equals 1, 5 over 5 equals 1 and just

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:14.530
any x over x is gonna equal 1 okay
so using that principle

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:18.810
we're gonna multiply by a factor
that helps break up

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:24.500
our numerator so we can simplify and then be

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:30.130
able to get that final answer and for
conjugates how it always works

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:35.150
is that you want to keep the same two terms but
change the sign in the middle so

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:40.410
here we're gonna keep our square root of 2x
plus 2h minus 1 and we're gonna

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:45.850
keep our square root of 2x minus 1 as well
but we're gonna have a plus

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:50.630
here instead of this minus and then obviously
so we can have this be the same as

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:54.210
we're multiplying by one we got to keep those
exact same whatever's in the numerator

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:58.910
we got to put in the denominator so you're
gonna have again 2x plus 2h minus 1

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:04.010
plus square root of 2x minus 1 okay now

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:10.310
because we multiply by a conjugate this will
break up super easily and we'll

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:15.160
just be left with the first term squared
minus the second term squared okay

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:20.630
it will become the square root of 2x

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:25.990
plus 2h minus 1 squared minus the square

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:29.810
root of 2x minus 1 all squared and

00:09:31.905 --> 00:09:35.535
then in the denominator we
are going to have

00:09:37.275 --> 00:09:42.885
our h multiplied by what was in the denominator
on that side, which is the square

00:09:42.735 --> 00:09:48.285
root of 2x plus 2h minus 1
plus the square root

00:09:48.135 --> 00:09:53.285
of 2x minus 1, okay? But this is always the
formula that's going to be. You're

00:09:53.135 --> 00:09:56.265
always going to have that first number squared,
that second number squared, both

00:09:56.115 --> 00:09:59.825
those terms, and you're going to have that
middle one eliminated because we had a

00:09:59.675 --> 00:10:03.865
negative and a positive on the other side
you're multiplying anyways though this

00:10:03.715 --> 00:10:09.295
will become the limit as h approaches 0 of if we
have a square root that square is

00:10:09.145 --> 00:10:13.915
the same as just that square root and that 2
will cancel out and we'll be left with

00:10:13.765 --> 00:10:18.715
2x plus 2h minus 1 then we're
gonna have minus

00:10:18.565 --> 00:10:21.455
2x minus 1

00:10:22.275 --> 00:10:27.165
all over h of the square root of 2x plus

00:10:27.015 --> 00:10:32.485
2h minus 1 plus the square
root of 2x minus 1,

00:10:32.515 --> 00:10:33.225
okay?

00:10:34.015 --> 00:10:37.765
And then here, if we have a 2x, and when we
apply this negative, it will become

00:10:37.615 --> 00:10:40.965
negative 2x, so this will cancel out, and that
will cancel out. And then here we

00:10:40.815 --> 00:10:44.225
have a negative 1, and then when we apply that
negative 1, it's going to be negative

00:10:44.075 --> 00:10:48.165
times negative, which will be positive 1, so
these two will also cancel out, and it

00:10:48.015 --> 00:10:51.625
will be left with the limit as
h approaches 0

00:10:52.595 --> 00:10:58.245
of 2h all over h times this huge

00:10:58.095 --> 00:10:58.965
middle guy here

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:09.540
okay and now we have an h in the
denominator that can be

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:14.360
factored out and we have one in the numerator so
we can divide these two and we will

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:19.380
get I'm gonna move this guy up here we're
gonna get equals the limit

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:25.160
as h approaches 0 of 2 over

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:30.040
the square root of 2x plus 2h minus 1

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:34.780
plus the square root of 2x minus 1, okay?

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:41.410
Now we can finally apply our limit. And the
reason we could now, even though there's

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:46.510
an h in the denominator and we couldn't earlier,
it's because here if we plug in the

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:51.150
h equals 0, it's going to be 0 multiplied by
this whole guy, which means it's going

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:55.670
to be 0 overall. And that 0 is in the
denominator. So again, we lose. It's undefined

00:11:55.520 --> 00:12:00.710
that's a no-go but because our h is in the
middle of terms that are being added and

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:06.160
under a square root this h if it goes to
zero our denominator will not go

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:11.460
to zero as you'll see here in just a sec so
because it's not going to zero we

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:16.330
can plug it in here and we'll be able to
solve and find our derivative

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:21.150
so here what's gonna happen when we plug in
zero for the h, we'll have 2 over

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:25.810
square root of 2x plus 2 times 0

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:30.410
minus 1 plus the square root
of 2x minus 1.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:35.770
This will become 0, and we're going to have the
square root of 2x minus 1 plus the

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:41.150
square root of 2x minus 1. That equals 2 over,
if you have two of the same thing,

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:46.530
it's going to become 2 times [the square root of]
2x minus 1, right? Because we have 2x minus 1 plus

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:51.910
2x minus 1 equals 2 times 2x minus
1. These two 2s will

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:56.730
reduce the fraction and we'll be left
with 1 over the square root of

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:58.390
2x minus 1.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:04.750
And that is our answer. Quick recap because
this was a lot of steps. We started

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:09.790
off by first getting our f of x plus h so we
can plug it into our OG formula.

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:16.170
Once we got it, we plugged in both those
numbers into our formula and we were not

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:20.710
able to simplify so we had to multiply by a
conjugate when we multiplied by this

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:24.850
conjugate it helped us square our first and
second term but it also left us with

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:28.490
some leftovers in the denominator because we
had to multiply h by the denominator

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:29.350
that was in our conjugate

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:35.370
from that we could subtract our like
terms and we were left with

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:40.700
2h over h times what was in the denominator from
our conjugate because there was an

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:45.180
h in the denominator and the numerator we were
able to cancel them out and be left

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:49.540
with that if we had an extra h in the
denominator, then we wouldn't have really done

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:53.900
anything because that h would have taken us to
zero and we would have had undefined.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:57.420
So we would have not been able to find the
derivative. But luckily we did.

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:03.680
After there was no more h being multiplied
into our conjugate, we were

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.020
able to apply that zero.

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:10.820
This term went to zero and we had 2 over [the square
root of] 2x minus 1 plus square root of 2x

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:15.380
minus 1. Again, that became 2 square root
of 2x minus 1, a 2 in the

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:19.180
numerator, a 2 in the [denominator] reduced and we are
left with this as our final answer

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:23.010
thank you very much and I'll see
you in the next one
